From 5d636161dc7593c2f8296250ad567bfb7aaafeed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Stosse <florian.stosse@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:37:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [wp] probes must not drop the variables of the goal

CfgWP.probe_vc replaced the free variables of the VC (vc.vars) with the
variables of the probed term only. These variables are used by
passify_vc (through occurs_vc) to decide which passive equalities of a
merge or label are relevant: once a probe was added, an equality such as
Mptr_0 = Mptr_1 between the pre-state and post-state memories of a chunk
the function never writes was dropped, because Mptr_1 only occurs in the
goal.

As a result, adding a probe (a 'probe' annotation, or the probes on the
formals generated by -wp-counter-examples) could turn a valid goal into
an unprovable one. For instance,
  ensures p->ptr == \old(p->ptr);
on a function writing only integer fields of *p is 'Prove: true' without
probes, and 'Prove: Mptr_0[a] = Mptr_1[a]' with no hypothesis relating
the two memories with them: Alt-Ergo times out, Z3 and CVC5 return
Unknown with a spurious model.

probe_vc now keeps vc.vars and adds the variables of the probe, as
assume_vc keeps them.

New test: wp_ce/probes_frame.i, with -wp-counter-examples and with a
probe annotation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 plugins/wp/src/cfgWP.ml                       |  2 +-
 .../wp_ce/oracle/probes_frame.0.res.oracle    | 72 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../wp_ce/oracle/probes_frame.1.res.oracle    | 72 +++++++++++++++++++
 plugins/wp/tests/wp_ce/probes_frame.i         | 41 +++++++++++
 4 files changed, 186 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 plugins/wp/tests/wp_ce/oracle/probes_frame.0.res.oracle
 create mode 100644 plugins/wp/tests/wp_ce/oracle/probes_frame.1.res.oracle
 create mode 100644 plugins/wp/tests/wp_ce/probes_frame.i

diff --git a/plugins/wp/src/cfgWP.ml b/plugins/wp/src/cfgWP.ml
index dc169d6daa..6d0152008d 100644
--- a/plugins/wp/src/cfgWP.ml
+++ b/plugins/wp/src/cfgWP.ml
@@ -288,7 +288,7 @@ struct
       }
 
   let probe_vc ~loc ?descr ?stmt ?warn ~name term vc =
-    let vars = F.vars term in
+    let vars = V.union (F.vars term) vc.vars in
     let hyps = Conditions.probe ~loc ?descr ?stmt ~name term vc.hyps in
     let wrns = match warn with
       | None -> vc.warn
